## 🛡️ Threat Model & Security Controls

| Threat Vector | Mitigation Strategy |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Server DB Leak** | Zero seed phrases or private keys exist on server DB. Server only holds public wallet address. |
| **Modified Local Vault** | AES-256-GCM authentication tag (`authTag`) integrity check rejects any altered bytes in IndexedDB. |
| **Wrong Password Attacks** | `Argon2id` memory-hard KDF prevents offline GPU brute-forcing; failed decryption throws `InvalidPasswordError`. |
| **XSS Session Theft** | Authentication tokens are stored in `HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Lax` cookies inaccessible to JavaScript. |
| **Memory Dump Attacks** | Active mnemonic buffers are explicitly zeroized (`buffer.fill(0)`) on lock, logout, or 10m idle timeout via `useVaultStore`. |
| **Brute-Force Auth Abuse** | Backend auth endpoints (`registerWallet`, `loginWallet`, `refreshSession`) enforce IP rate-limiting. |

